  It can, but xorxes point' was that "roxy.xipa" is a single numeric
string, all-X(1)  (remember that "paxy." -> "1X" is considered a number, an=
d
can do all things that numbers do (quantify sumti, etc.)).  Since you want
to make this two different "words" you have to end the quantifier part with
a boi, "ro boi xy xi pa", the same as you have to do if you want to say, fo=
r
example, "xy boi zy  darxi" if you mean "X hits Z", and not "xy zy darxi"
("XZ hits")

  (Of course, jboski/genrei chokes on "xy xi pa" for reasons unknown to me,
but there is nothing wrong with it grammatically

           --gejyspa



